# The Dockerfile reads only Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/, LICENSE and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Everything else is build context the daemon uploads and
# then ignores — on a working tree that has been built and tested locally that is
# several GB (target/ alone reaches 6-10 GB), which is the difference between a
# fast build and one that looks hung.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded, because the runtime stage copies them:
#   LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md,
#   crates/iaga-sentinel-core/iaga-sentinel.example.yaml,
#   crates/iaga-sentinel-dictum/examples, crates/iaga-sentinel-core/examples/policies

# Build output and dependency trees — the bulk of the context
target/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/dist/

# VCS
.git/
.github/

# Local state that must never reach an image layer
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-journal
**/chain.json
**/.env
**/.local/
**/.live/
**/keys/

# Trees the build never reads
docs/
sdks/
plug-ins/
charts/
deploy/
scripts/
